A||N||9||superXmotorsports||best way to remove sail panels||||1||
Z||000000||superXmotorsports||12-20-1999||04:44 PM||||Does anybody know an easy way to remove the sail panles on a fastback GT w/ out damaging them?  Thanks!  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||05:47 PM||||Without damaging them?  I guess that rules out sledge hammers and crowbars <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||12-20-1999||07:48 PM||||I'd like to know as well. I'm getting the FOCOA scooped quarter windows for my GT for Christmas and I don't want to damage them putting them in. ||||reg||5
Z||000003||fieroshop||12-20-1999||08:50 PM||||SXM,<BR>Get a small stranded cable and push it thru at ane end, then very slowly worked it back and forth like a saw and work your way around the window until you have it all off. Before you put it back on you must clean the double sided tape that you just cut off completly and clean the area where the tape was before you put the new one on.||||reg||6
Z||000004||JetroGT||12-21-1999||01:32 PM||||It would also help if you removed them on a hot day or in a heated garage.||||reg||1
Z||000005||superXmotorsports||12-21-1999||06:46 PM||||Thanks for the advise!||||reg||14
Z||000006||AL||12-21-1999||10:21 PM||||hey gokart, are you going to need your old sail panels once you've replaced them with the others? if not ill take them if you don't mind.||||reg||7
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||12-21-1999||11:19 PM||||There is a string installed behind the adhesive from the factory. If you can get a hold of it on a warm day you should have no trouble. I recently got a fastback clip and detroyed the 1/4 windows removing thme, then I saw the string. DOH!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tom88gt||12-23-1999||06:09 PM||||Do any of you know how to research up old Kit Car/KIT CAR ILLUSTRATED magazine articles?  A couple/few years ago I read a VERY detailed article on removing the entire body.  Lots of pictures too.  Wish I still had the magazine.  If you contact these magazines they should have archives.  Wish I had a better idea of when the article was.  <P>Also try one of the kit makers.  They will have instructions on removing the body.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||12-23-1999||07:36 PM||||Sure Al! There not cracked or broken, just splintered from the sun, I guess? You pay shipping and there yours. Only thing is I'm not sure exactly when I'll do this project with the cold weather setting in!||||reg||6
